<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Framework overlay - Meizu M6 (meizu_m6 / M711).

  DELIBERATELY ALMOST EMPTY, and that is the finding, not an omission.

  The LineageOS 16.0 tree that boots this device has NO
  overlay/frameworks/base/core/res overlay at all - its only overlay is
  packages/apps/Camera2/res/values/config.xml (verified by listing
  gunwest-import/m6rom16/rom-work/device/meizu/meizu_m6/overlay). So there are no
  measured auto-brightness curves for this panel to carry over, the way m681 and
  l681 have. Inventing curves for a panel whose identity is itself unresolved
  (ili9881c on the live unit vs ili9881p on the dead one, see BoardConfig.mk)
  would be exactly the cargo cult this fleet's rules forbid.

  The two booleans below are safe device facts rather than tuning:
    config_showNavigationBar - FACT: the LOS16 system.prop sets
      qemu.hw.mainkeys=0 and the mBack hardware key is driven by a vendor
      fingerprint blob stack (goodixfingerprintd + gf-keys.kl) that this tree
      does not ship, so without the on-screen bar there is no way back.
    config_hotswapCapable - FACT: dual SIM with a hot-swappable tray;
      ro.telephony.sim.count=2 in the existing system.prop, and the stock fstab
      declares sdcard1 as voldmanaged=auto on a shared tray.

  Both names were checked against this tree's
  frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/{config,symbols}.xml.
-->
<resources>
    <bool name="config_showNavigationBar">true</bool>
    <bool name="config_hotswapCapable">true</bool>
</resources>
